== review-report.md format ==
# Review Report — Round {{.Round}}
## Summary
PASS / FAIL
## Checklist
| Item | Status | Notes |
## Issues
### [SEVERITY] Rule — file/path
Description
## Verdict
PASS / FAIL / CONDITIONAL PASS

== Severity ==
- critical/HIGH: blocks transition, must fix
- warning/MEDIUM: should fix
- low/INFO: log only

== Incremental Writing & Resume ==
Write review-report.md incrementally — create the file with the header and empty table first,
then update it after each checklist item reviewed. Do not accumulate everything in memory and
write once at the end.

Before starting, check if review-report.md already exists. A previous session may have been
interrupted mid-review. If it exists, read it:
- Items already in the checklist table with a Status → already reviewed, skip them
- Empty rows or missing items → review these (this is where the previous session stopped)
- A file with only headers or an empty table means resume from the first item
- If Verdict is already filled → the review is complete, verify it's consistent and finish
Do NOT assume an existing file means the review is done — check which items have results.

